  "id": "religious-therapy",
  "term": "religious therapy",
  "definition": "Religious therapy refers to using religious practices or sacred elements, such as holy water, as a way of coping with illness, including mental health problems. In this context, it describes a faith-based approach people may turn to alongside their experience of symptoms.",
